This is one of the most important design decisions.
Don't create:
RSI = BUY
MACD = BUY
EMA = BUY
Supertrend = BUY
SMC = BUY
ICT = BUY
AI = BUY

Therefore BUY
That creates correlated signals and can give you false confidence.
Instead create independent analytical layers.

Layer A — Price
OHLC
Candlestick structure
Support/resistance
Trendlines
Breakouts
Retests
Gaps
Volatility

Layer B — Market Structure
HH/HL
LH/LL
BOS
CHOCH/MSS
Swing structure
Trend state

Layer C — SMC
Order blocks
Fair value gaps
Liquidity pools
Equal highs/lows
Liquidity sweeps
Displacement
Premium/discount
Mitigation

Layer D — ICT-style concepts
Liquidity
Market structure shifts
FVG
OTE
Kill zones/session concepts
Dealing ranges
PD arrays

These need precise deterministic definitions, not vague chart interpretations

Layer E — Classical TA
EMA/SMA
RSI
MACD
ADX
ATR
Bollinger Bands
Stochastic
VWAP
Ichimoku
Fibonacci

Layer F — Volume
Volume profile
VWAP
Relative volume
OBV
Volume delta where available
Cumulative volume measures

Layer G — Options
Option chain
OI
OI change
IV
IV rank
Put/call ratios
Bid/ask
Volume
Greeks
Max pain as a contextual feature, not a standalone signal
Expiry structure
Strike-wise positioning

Layer H — Macro
Interest rates
Inflation
Currency
Crude
Gold
Global indices
Economic calendar
Central-bank events

Layer I — News/Sentiment
News classification
Event detection
Sentiment
Entity impact
Surprise detection




